cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "In-silico drug discovery toolkit: multi-endpoint ADMET and pharmacology prediction"
message: "If you use this toolkit or its models, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yasini-Ardekani
    given-names: Nabil
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/abinittio/Insilico-Drug-Discovery-Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  An integrated in-silico platform for early-stage drug discovery covering
  monoamine transporter (DAT/NET/SERT) activity classification, abuse liability,
  hERG cardiotoxicity, CYP450 metabolism and blood-brain barrier permeability,
  with a SMARTS-based pharmacology rules engine for known failure modes.
  Reported metrics are scaffold-split and in-dataset unless stated otherwise.
keywords:
  - ADMET
  - drug discovery
  - cheminformatics
  - graph neural networks
  - monoamine transporters
license: MIT
